1
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:37,151
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,151 --> 00:02:41,151
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,151 --> 00:02:45,151
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,151 --> 00:02:50,151
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,151 --> 00:02:53,151
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,151 --> 00:02:56,151
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,151 --> 00:02:59,151
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,151 --> 00:03:02,151
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:03,151 --> 00:03:06,151
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:06,151 --> 00:03:09,151
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,151 --> 00:03:12,151
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:17,151
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,151 --> 00:03:22,151
Separated from the rest of his crew,

14
00:03:22,151 --> 00:03:26,151
Luffy has finally arrived at Marineford to rescue his brother Ace.

15
00:03:26,151 --> 00:03:29,151
The White Beard Pirates have successfully pushed into the bay,

16
00:03:29,151 --> 00:03:32,151
but a massive number of Marines still block the path to Ace.

17
00:03:32,151 --> 00:03:34,151
The battle is heating up.

18
00:03:37,151 --> 00:03:39,151
Apologies, Shanks.

19
00:03:41,151 --> 00:03:44,151
But I will not hold back against him.

20
00:03:44,151 --> 00:03:47,151
Hey, I know him! Hawkeye!

21
00:03:47,151 --> 00:03:50,151
I wonder what is written.

22
00:03:50,151 --> 00:03:53,151
Will my hand wipe his name from history?

23
00:03:53,151 --> 00:04:00,151
Or perhaps his fortune shall spare him the fury of this black sword I wield?

24
00:04:05,151 --> 00:04:07,151
The Great Swordsman Mihawk!

25
00:04:07,151 --> 00:04:10,151
Luffy comes under the attack of the Black Sword!

26
00:04:14,151 --> 00:04:17,151
I don't have time to get in a fight with such a strong guy!

27
00:04:18,151 --> 00:04:20,151
All I'm here to do is save Ace!

28
00:04:26,151 --> 00:04:28,151
Go! Second gear!

29
00:04:28,151 --> 00:04:29,151
Yeah!

30
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:39,151
Yee-haw! Death! Wink!

31
00:04:44,151 --> 00:04:46,151
Galaxy! Wink!

32
00:04:52,151 --> 00:04:54,151
That's it, Straw Boy, well done.

33
00:04:54,151 --> 00:04:57,151
Just keep your eyes on the prize and keep moving forward.

34
00:04:57,151 --> 00:04:59,151
You let us handle the rest.

35
00:05:05,151 --> 00:05:08,151
Don't worry, we'll deal with fancy pants!

36
00:05:08,151 --> 00:05:09,151
Yee-haw!

37
00:05:09,151 --> 00:05:10,151
Yeah!

38
00:05:11,151 --> 00:05:12,151
Hey, Hawkeye!

39
00:05:12,151 --> 00:05:14,151
Remember the time we challenged you?

40
00:05:14,151 --> 00:05:17,151
Well, here comes a blast of the past to kick your smug ass!

41
00:05:17,151 --> 00:05:26,151
We're powered up now as newcomers, and you're gonna feel it!

42
00:05:32,151 --> 00:05:34,151
I don't remember you.

43
00:05:34,151 --> 00:05:37,151
Your worms in a long line of them.

44
00:05:37,151 --> 00:05:55,151
Almost there! Keep running, and don't look back!

45
00:05:55,151 --> 00:05:56,151
Whoa!

46
00:05:56,151 --> 00:05:57,151
What?

47
00:05:57,151 --> 00:05:58,151
You're still... in range.

48
00:05:59,151 --> 00:06:00,151
Whoa!

49
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:01,151
Whoa!

50
00:06:06,151 --> 00:06:07,151
Yaa-hah!

51
00:06:07,151 --> 00:06:08,151
Yaa-hah!

52
00:06:08,151 --> 00:06:09,151
You're still... in range.

53
00:06:11,151 --> 00:06:12,151
Yaaa-hah!

54
00:06:13,151 --> 00:06:14,151
Yaa-hah!

55
00:06:14,151 --> 00:06:25,291
Oh, man.

56
00:06:26,291 --> 00:06:27,231
He got me.

57
00:06:30,451 --> 00:06:33,351
Only Ace's brother could survive that attack.

58
00:06:33,791 --> 00:06:36,151
Anyone else would have been sliced clean in half.

59
00:06:36,631 --> 00:06:38,411
The turncoat gene bag.

60
00:06:39,051 --> 00:06:42,571
I'm going to make sure that's the last time you so much as touch, Luffy.

61
00:06:42,571 --> 00:06:45,031
Even if it costs me my life.

62
00:06:45,811 --> 00:06:47,391
Why are you doing this?

63
00:06:47,691 --> 00:06:50,251
For one, I don't want to see Ace get murdered.

64
00:06:50,631 --> 00:06:53,051
And I'd like to have a peaceful sea for a change.

65
00:06:53,391 --> 00:06:57,031
It may be too late to avoid the war we've gotten ourselves into now.

66
00:06:57,371 --> 00:06:58,831
But there is still hope.

67
00:06:59,471 --> 00:07:02,291
Namely, in that daring kid over there.

68
00:07:04,771 --> 00:07:05,831
Hope, you say.

69
00:07:06,471 --> 00:07:08,671
We'll see what fate lies in store for him.

70
00:07:09,351 --> 00:07:11,811
But as for you, I'd step back.

71
00:07:11,811 --> 00:07:13,811
Fishman Karate.

72
00:07:17,811 --> 00:07:20,811
Arabesque Brick Fist.

73
00:07:36,811 --> 00:07:39,191
Sharkskin All Frost.

74
00:07:39,191 --> 00:07:43,551
Shark Brick Fist.

75
00:08:00,191 --> 00:08:02,131
That guy's a monster.

76
00:08:02,131 --> 00:08:10,131
He's going in for the kill.

77
00:08:10,131 --> 00:08:10,591
He's going in for the kill.

78
00:08:10,591 --> 00:08:35,871
Nobody wants to kill him.

79
00:08:35,871 --> 00:08:43,591
Too close.

80
00:08:43,791 --> 00:08:46,131
He'd have sliced my arms right off if I'd attacked.

81
00:08:46,471 --> 00:08:48,511
So, you're smarter than you look.

82
00:08:52,511 --> 00:08:55,511
Oh, no.

83
00:09:05,871 --> 00:09:17,831
Okay, the sword should not do that.

84
00:09:18,051 --> 00:09:21,171
Could we please call that thing something other than the sword?

85
00:09:24,851 --> 00:09:28,111
He's definitely earned that world's strongest swordsman title.

86
00:09:30,571 --> 00:09:32,571
He's stronger than a mountain of ice.

87
00:09:32,691 --> 00:09:34,751
There's no way Straw Hat's going to survive.

88
00:09:34,751 --> 00:09:36,171
None of he's fighting here.

89
00:09:42,251 --> 00:09:45,271
That's why you don't slice Ice Marks!

90
00:09:57,651 --> 00:09:59,131
Still need footsteps.

91
00:09:59,391 --> 00:10:00,571
No one sees me.

92
00:10:00,571 --> 00:10:05,071
All right, you guys ready?

93
00:10:05,491 --> 00:10:10,211
Time to put Operation Make Captain Buggy look like a badass in front of the world into action.

94
00:10:10,591 --> 00:10:14,211
The Navy loves propaganda, so I'm sure they're broadcasting the war.

95
00:10:14,491 --> 00:10:17,251
We just gotta find us a video transponder snail.

96
00:10:17,751 --> 00:10:18,611
Let's go!

97
00:10:18,611 --> 00:10:26,331
It's shocking how easy it is to encourage them with such vague directions.

98
00:10:26,331 --> 00:10:36,811
So you want to team up?

99
00:10:36,811 --> 00:10:37,451
Nonsense.

100
00:10:37,451 --> 00:10:38,451
Why not?

101
00:10:38,451 --> 00:10:38,951
Why not?

102
00:10:38,951 --> 00:10:43,251
The reign of these antiquated geriatric pirates like Whitebeard is coming to an end.

103
00:10:43,251 --> 00:10:44,951
He's the last of them.

104
00:10:44,951 --> 00:10:48,371
We're on the brink of a new era, and it belongs to us.

105
00:10:48,371 --> 00:10:52,051
An era where all that matters is the power you yield.

106
00:10:52,051 --> 00:10:54,091
Sounds appealing, right?

107
00:10:54,091 --> 00:10:55,971
You know you want a piece of it.

108
00:10:58,971 --> 00:11:00,271
Oh, come on now.

109
00:11:00,351 --> 00:11:01,891
I can tell that you're intrigued.

110
00:11:04,231 --> 00:11:11,151
Sure, technically you've been stripped of your title, but when you get down to it, we're both warlords at heart, aren't we?

111
00:11:11,151 --> 00:11:15,751
Stop looking at me like you're my equal, cause you're far from it.

112
00:11:16,531 --> 00:11:19,171
If anything, you should be begging to work for me.

113
00:11:20,831 --> 00:11:27,071
Well then, and here I thought you'd been humbled by prison, but not even impelled down could make a dent in you.

114
00:11:28,451 --> 00:11:29,111
Damn straight.

115
00:11:29,211 --> 00:11:30,791
I've heard enough talk.

116
00:11:31,251 --> 00:11:31,831
Sables!

117
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:35,831
Get lost, you jacko!

118
00:11:41,151 --> 00:11:49,351
I assumed you could be reasoned with, but I was obviously mistaken.

119
00:11:52,771 --> 00:11:55,931
These dumb jawheads don't notice you if you don't try to fight them.

120
00:11:56,351 --> 00:11:58,151
We can just breathe through.

121
00:12:06,151 --> 00:12:08,371
Freeze! Get in the game!

122
00:12:08,371 --> 00:12:12,971
Whoa! He literally got sucked into someone else's might!

123
00:12:15,271 --> 00:12:19,231
Are you gonna move, or do I have to make you? What'll it be?

124
00:12:19,571 --> 00:12:24,211
You're welcome to try, but you will perish before I let you touch my future husband.

125
00:12:25,031 --> 00:12:25,511
Husband?

126
00:12:26,531 --> 00:12:28,771
Yes, my betrothed.

127
00:12:31,891 --> 00:12:35,251
After this ceremony, we'll embark upon an enchanted honeymoon.

128
00:12:35,251 --> 00:12:47,071
Luffy, my love, let us abscond into the depths of amorous euphoria.

129
00:12:47,071 --> 00:12:55,931
But then, what if?

130
00:12:56,771 --> 00:12:59,311
Our bliss has left me famished, my dear.

131
00:12:59,491 --> 00:13:01,851
I'm afraid the food storage is empty, darling.

132
00:13:02,411 --> 00:13:05,251
But the world is full of meals waiting to be cooked.

133
00:13:06,231 --> 00:13:10,651
My darling, cook for me so I can taste your love.

134
00:13:10,971 --> 00:13:11,591
Of course.

135
00:13:12,251 --> 00:13:13,191
Anything for you.

136
00:13:13,651 --> 00:13:15,351
Just give me one moment, darling.

137
00:13:15,351 --> 00:13:19,631
I must be prepared for this possibility.

138
00:13:20,611 --> 00:13:22,351
Luffy's appetite is truly voracious.

139
00:13:22,931 --> 00:13:26,951
If I want to satisfy him, I must be capable of producing a truly colossal feast.

140
00:13:31,631 --> 00:13:32,831
Please make, princess!

141
00:13:33,231 --> 00:13:34,951
We'll be happy to make it for you!

142
00:13:35,411 --> 00:13:36,651
I'll have nothing of it.

143
00:13:37,091 --> 00:13:40,091
Luffy wants to savor the labors of my love, not yours.

144
00:13:40,931 --> 00:13:43,651
Darling, how much longer must I wait?

145
00:13:43,651 --> 00:13:47,251
It's coming, my love.

146
00:13:47,571 --> 00:13:49,391
Such a dying devotion!

147
00:13:50,091 --> 00:13:54,411
I'll gladly embrace any trouble that life throws our way, because it's worth it.

148
00:13:55,011 --> 00:13:56,611
Anything's worth it to be his wife.

149
00:13:57,851 --> 00:13:58,651
His wife!

150
00:13:58,651 --> 00:14:01,011
What the hell?

151
00:14:01,211 --> 00:14:03,551
I can't tell if she wants to fight me or not.

152
00:14:05,531 --> 00:14:06,011
Straw Hat!

153
00:14:06,231 --> 00:14:06,951
Got you!

154
00:14:07,071 --> 00:14:09,091
Are you deaf, you ridiculous fool?

155
00:14:09,311 --> 00:14:11,511
The only way you're getting past me is in a coffin!

156
00:14:12,151 --> 00:14:13,271
Perfume fever!

157
00:14:14,191 --> 00:14:15,271
You're kidding me.

158
00:14:15,571 --> 00:14:15,891
Really?

159
00:14:20,991 --> 00:14:22,051
Stop now!

160
00:14:22,051 --> 00:14:32,931
You'll never make it to your brother in time!

161
00:14:37,551 --> 00:14:39,371
You shall perish after all!

162
00:14:39,371 --> 00:14:58,171
Just freezing through!

163
00:14:58,331 --> 00:14:59,431
Nothing strange here!

164
00:14:59,431 --> 00:15:02,531
There's no denying his fighting skills have improved.

165
00:15:02,871 --> 00:15:04,611
Well, I've already seen all his moves.

166
00:15:04,891 --> 00:15:06,531
There's no chance that I'll miss again.

167
00:15:06,711 --> 00:15:08,191
Not from such a close distance.

168
00:15:10,271 --> 00:15:11,571
Don't find me!

169
00:15:11,691 --> 00:15:12,811
Just passing through!

170
00:15:12,891 --> 00:15:13,791
Come, come!

171
00:15:14,151 --> 00:15:14,371
Yeah!

172
00:15:15,151 --> 00:15:15,391
Oh!

173
00:15:15,811 --> 00:15:16,571
Nice save!

174
00:15:18,831 --> 00:15:20,451
Jet human, chill!

175
00:15:20,991 --> 00:15:22,971
Hey, what's wrong with you?

176
00:15:23,571 --> 00:15:24,471
I'll die!

177
00:15:25,471 --> 00:15:25,871
What?

178
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,451
I didn't slice you!

179
00:15:27,731 --> 00:15:29,311
Besides, I just heard you say,

180
00:15:29,431 --> 00:15:30,311
don't mind me!

181
00:15:30,471 --> 00:15:31,471
I'm here to save you!

182
00:15:31,491 --> 00:15:34,391
There is no way your hearing is that selfishly selective!

183
00:15:35,331 --> 00:15:36,471
Gum gum!

184
00:15:36,791 --> 00:15:37,991
Human shield!

185
00:15:38,151 --> 00:15:39,151
Cut it out!

186
00:15:44,251 --> 00:15:45,591
All right!

187
00:15:45,851 --> 00:15:46,351
Enough!

188
00:15:46,491 --> 00:15:47,831
Your sword's not working!

189
00:15:48,751 --> 00:15:50,791
Suffer the special muggy ball!

190
00:15:50,931 --> 00:15:52,071
And blow off!

191
00:15:54,471 --> 00:15:56,451
Or maybe not.

192
00:15:56,651 --> 00:15:58,151
Do you want to hear a joke instead?

193
00:15:58,551 --> 00:16:01,191
How's the muggy ball like a robust financial market?

194
00:16:01,511 --> 00:16:02,191
I don't know.

195
00:16:02,271 --> 00:16:02,831
How is it?

196
00:16:02,891 --> 00:16:03,991
Say it together, everyone.

197
00:16:04,251 --> 00:16:05,511
Because it goes...

198
00:16:05,511 --> 00:16:09,691
I've never heard that one before!

199
00:16:09,911 --> 00:16:10,931
Nice, Captain Buggy.

200
00:16:10,971 --> 00:16:11,571
Good one!

201
00:16:12,431 --> 00:16:13,791
Thank you, Buggy!

202
00:16:14,511 --> 00:16:16,951
See you in the afterlife, I guess!

203
00:16:17,031 --> 00:16:17,951
We're not done!

204
00:16:17,951 --> 00:16:27,771
Vista, Pop said to make sure Ace's brother doesn't get killed.

205
00:16:27,931 --> 00:16:28,511
Now go!

206
00:16:28,851 --> 00:16:29,571
Back him up!

207
00:16:29,831 --> 00:16:30,311
Certainly!

208
00:16:30,611 --> 00:16:31,751
I shall make haste!

209
00:16:31,751 --> 00:16:41,531
We meet at last.

210
00:16:41,671 --> 00:16:44,151
Your reputation precedes you, Flower Sword Vista.

211
00:16:44,971 --> 00:16:47,051
It's a pleasure to meet you, too!

212
00:16:48,011 --> 00:16:49,851
I'm thrilled you've heard of me!

213
00:16:50,691 --> 00:16:53,091
You can drop the false modesty.

214
00:16:53,091 --> 00:16:57,791
Oh, well, that sucked!

215
00:16:58,391 --> 00:16:59,371
That mustache guy!

216
00:16:59,591 --> 00:17:00,211
Who is he?

217
00:17:00,491 --> 00:17:02,831
I see Straw Hat's true strength.

218
00:17:03,351 --> 00:17:04,871
Well, thanks, whoever you are!

219
00:17:04,871 --> 00:17:30,971
It's nothing to do with physical strength.

220
00:17:31,211 --> 00:17:33,471
His power is to rally those around him.

221
00:17:34,871 --> 00:17:38,451
That's the spirit, Straw Boy!

222
00:17:38,751 --> 00:17:39,551
Keep running!

223
00:17:41,231 --> 00:17:43,351
At least he got past me, Honk.

224
00:17:45,531 --> 00:17:46,051
Muffy!

225
00:17:46,691 --> 00:17:47,671
Save your brother!

226
00:17:47,831 --> 00:17:48,711
You can do it!

227
00:17:51,571 --> 00:17:53,211
Out of my way!

228
00:17:54,911 --> 00:17:57,911
Of all the people seeking to conquer the sea,

229
00:17:57,911 --> 00:18:04,591
he may possess the greatest talent of all.

230
00:18:04,871 --> 00:18:05,491
Ace!

231
00:18:05,491 --> 00:18:05,871
Not again!

232
00:18:05,871 --> 00:18:06,531
That...

233
00:18:06,531 --> 00:18:18,311
That damn straw hat you'll pay for me!

234
00:18:18,311 --> 00:18:22,091
Once again, you've proven how amazing you are!

235
00:18:22,091 --> 00:18:23,771
You let Hawkeye think he'd beaten you,

236
00:18:23,771 --> 00:18:26,671
but in reality, you got exactly what you wanted!

237
00:18:26,671 --> 00:18:27,671
Huh?

238
00:18:27,671 --> 00:18:28,671
What do you mean?

239
00:18:28,671 --> 00:18:30,271
Don't be so coy.

240
00:18:30,271 --> 00:18:31,311
You did it, Captain!

241
00:18:31,311 --> 00:18:34,711
A video transponder snail?

242
00:18:35,711 --> 00:18:36,631
Uh, yeah!

243
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:38,811
That was definitely my plan.

244
00:18:38,971 --> 00:18:41,171
But did you expect anything less from the man

245
00:18:41,171 --> 00:18:42,411
who's gonna rule the world?

246
00:18:42,411 --> 00:18:43,751
Ha-ha-ha!

247
00:18:43,751 --> 00:18:47,751
I'll follow you to the end of time, Captain Buggy!

248
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:48,751
Bye!

249
00:18:48,751 --> 00:18:49,751
Shh!

250
00:18:49,751 --> 00:18:50,751
Yeah!

251
00:18:50,751 --> 00:18:54,971
Now, this is where the important part starts.

252
00:18:54,971 --> 00:18:58,591
I wish that the universe would stop encouraging him.

253
00:18:58,591 --> 00:19:03,591
In the looming shadow of Ace's impending execution,

254
00:19:03,591 --> 00:19:07,591
the world has been rocked by one revelation after another.

255
00:19:07,591 --> 00:19:17,091
It all began when more than 200 inmates managed to escape

256
00:19:17,091 --> 00:19:19,471
from the iron-tight prison of Impel Down,

257
00:19:19,471 --> 00:19:21,471
and the most notorious of those prisoners

258
00:19:21,471 --> 00:19:24,351
have now taken a lead role in this epic battle.

259
00:19:28,351 --> 00:19:31,251
The blood-soaked expanse of the ghastly battlefield

260
00:19:31,251 --> 00:19:33,351
is an unearthly sight,

261
00:19:33,351 --> 00:19:35,411
and with a single glance at its horrors,

262
00:19:35,411 --> 00:19:38,751
it's clear that this showdown will change history.

263
00:19:48,491 --> 00:19:50,651
The populace of the world has no choice

264
00:19:50,651 --> 00:19:53,171
but to helplessly observe the events of this war

265
00:19:53,171 --> 00:19:54,871
with the knowledge that its outcome

266
00:19:54,871 --> 00:19:56,871
will determine their very future.

267
00:20:05,411 --> 00:20:08,371
flight admiral, everything has been arranged!

268
00:20:08,371 --> 00:20:09,751
The bay is fully prepared as well.

